@startuml
title Parking Domain, Live Samples, and Historical Coverage
skinparam packageStyle rectangle

enum HistoryResolution {
  AUTO
  TEN_MINUTE
  ONE_HOUR
  SIX_HOUR
  TWELVE_HOUR
  TWENTY_FOUR_HOUR
}

enum BackfillState {
  PROCESSING
  RETRY_WAIT
  COMPLETE
}

class ParkingDay <<Mongo document>> {
  facilityId : int
  sydneyDate : String (YYYY-MM-DD)
  samples : List<Sample>
  backfillState : BackfillState?
  retryAfter : Instant?
  leaseUntil : Instant?
  completedAt : Instant?
}

class Sample <<embedded value>> {
  bucketIndex : int
  sourceTime : Instant
  occupancy : int
  capacity : int
}

class ParkingDayKey <<logical key>> {
  facilityId : int
  sydneyDate : LocalDate
}

class SydneyDayClock {
  + startOfDay(date : LocalDate) : Instant
  + bucketTime(date : LocalDate, index : int) : Instant
}

class UpstreamTimeMapper {
  - fromSydneyMessageDate(messageDate : LocalDateTime) : Instant
}

class CurrentCarParkFeed {
  GET /carpark?facility={id}
  returns latest record
}

class HistoricalCarParkFeed {
  GET /carpark/history?facility={id}&eventdate={date}
  returns history records
}

ParkingDay "1" *-- "0..150" Sample
ParkingDay ..> ParkingDayKey : unique index
Sample ..> SydneyDayClock : bucket index is 10 min
CurrentCarParkFeed ..> UpstreamTimeMapper : MessageDate
HistoricalCarParkFeed ..> UpstreamTimeMapper : MessageDate; eventdate is only a fetch key
UpstreamTimeMapper ..> Sample : Sydney local -> UTC Instant

note right of ParkingDay
  One document per (facilityId, Sydney calendar date).
  Query by facilityId + sydneyDate; do not derive the
  calendar key by truncating a UTC instant.

  samples is bounded to one latest observation per
  10-minute Sydney bucket (max 150 for a 25-hour day).
  bucketIndex is relative to Sydney start of day;
  bucket time is startOfDay(date) + index * 10 min.

  Historical coverage state shares the daily record, but live refresh
  does not set it COMPLETE. Mark COMPLETE only after every upstream
  eventdate segment required for that Sydney date has succeeded.
end note

note bottom of Sample
  Store sourceTime as a UTC Instant/BSON date. Within a bucket,
  retain the newest sourceTime so late arrivals cannot overwrite it.
  MessageDate is Sydney local time and is the source of truth for
  sydneyDate. Ignore the legacy `time` field for timestamp conversion.
  API timestamps are computed from Sydney date + bucketIndex,
  then serialized as epoch milliseconds.
end note

note left of BackfillState
  Missing state means not requested. PROCESSING uses leaseUntil;
  RETRY_WAIT uses retryAfter; COMPLETE means historical provider-date
  coverage for the Sydney day is complete. A live response or an empty
  partial history response cannot complete the historical day.
  No separate status object/collection.
end note
@enduml
